<h1>filename_path</h1>
<p>Using this function returns the path part of the indicated file path, including the final backslash.</p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Syntax:</h4>
<p class="code">filename_path(fname);</p>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th>Argument</th><th>Type</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>fname</td><td><span data-keyref="Type_String"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">String</a></span></td>
<td>The file name and path to use.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p> </p>
<h4>Returns:</h4>
<p class="code"><span data-keyref="Type_String"><a target="_blank" href="../../../GML_Overview/Data_Types.htm">String</a></span></p>
<p> </p>
<h4>Example:</h4>
<p class="code">path = filename_path(working_directory + &quot;Test.ini&quot;);</p>
<p>The above code gets the path (as a string) of the specified file.</p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
<p> </p>
